    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c9f45bb5",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: forgive_me_allah_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a man prostrating himself on a prayer rug in what appears to be a public setting, surrounded by police and onlookers. The overlaid text reads: 'forgive me allah.. i just can't understand why i am allowed to behead my enemies and marry little girls, but i can't eat a fucking ham sandwich.' This text is intentionally provocative and hateful, using a juxtaposition of religious piety with extreme, violent, and sexually charged accusations against Islam. It leverages the visual of a Muslim man in prayer to mock Islamic religious practices and cultural norms, particularly by framing the consumption of pork as a 'sin' while simultaneously implying that other acts (beheading enemies, marrying young girls) are 'allowed' or 'acceptable' within the faith. This is a clear example of Islamophobia, as it directly attacks the perceived moral and religious framework of Islam by mocking its practices and associating them with barbarism and hypocrisy. The meme's intent is to provoke outrage, ridicule, and reinforce negative stereotypes about Muslims, making it a hateful and harmful piece of content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_435a890e"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
